ity, decision quality, crew atmosphere. Concerns: communication, egocentric, education.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership, weak leadership, arrogance. Strengths: adaptability, concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: arrogance, weak leadership.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely candidate C has reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation. Candidate B has stress resilience and conscientiousness but uncooperative and grumpy. Candidate A has anticipation and technical vision but organization and criticism issues. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nProbably candidate C is strongest overall because reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere are crucial. Communication difficulty is a concern but crew atmosphere positive suggests maybe can manage. I'd propose candidate C.\n\nNow produce public message: state recommendation for Candidate C, reference discussion (none yet) but we can say \"Given the criteria, I think C stands out because...\". Provide facts. Provide implication.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
